# AGENTS.md

Context for AI coding agents working in this repository.

## Project

{{ project_name }} — a FastAPI full-stack app generated by [flint](https://github.com/abdulazeezoj/flint).
Pages are rendered server-side with Jinja2; interactivity (the Todo
list's add/toggle/delete) is HTMX partial-swaps, not a client-side JS
framework — every route returns either a full page or an HTML fragment,
never JSON.

## Setup

```
uv sync
```

## Run

```
uv run fastapi dev src/{{ package_name }}/main.py
```
{% if migrations %}
Apply migrations first: `uv run alembic upgrade head`.
{% endif %}
{% if worker == "taskiq" %}
Run the worker (separate process): `uv run taskiq worker {{ package_name }}.worker:broker --app-dir src`.
{% elif worker == "celery" %}
Run the worker (separate process): `PYTHONPATH=src uv run celery -A {{ package_name }}.worker.celery_app worker --loglevel=info`.
{% endif %}
{% if css == "tailwind" %}
Build the CSS first, or the page has no styling: `uv run tailwindcss -i
src/{{ package_name }}/static/css/input.css -o
src/{{ package_name }}/static/css/style.css` (add `--watch` while iterating
on templates).
{% endif %}

## Test

```
uv run pytest
```

## Layout

Two fixed entrypoints, two "add a resource here" folders, one folder for
shared infrastructure — the rest is unopinionated (borrowed from how
Next.js only enforces structure for routing, nothing else):

- `src/{{ package_name }}/main.py` — **the** FastAPI entrypoint: `app`,
  lifespan, mounted routers, the `/static` mount. Don't rename or move it.
- `src/{{ package_name }}/routes/` — **one module per HTTP resource.**
  `todos.py` is the example; a new resource is a new file here plus one
  `app.include_router(...)` line in `main.py`.
- `src/{{ package_name }}/templates/` — Jinja2 templates, rendered via
  `core/templates.py`'s shared `templates` instance. `base.html` is the
  shell (HTMX script tag, stylesheet); `index.html` is the Todo page;
  `partials/` holds the fragments routes return directly for HTMX swaps
  (`todo_item.html`, `empty_state.html`, `todo_created.html`).
- `src/{{ package_name }}/static/` — served at `/static` by the
  `StaticFiles` mount in `main.py`.{% if css == "tailwind" %} `css/input.css` is
  the Tailwind source (edit this, plus template class names); `css/style.css`
  is the **built, git-ignored** output — rebuild it after any change (see
  "Run" above) or edits won't show up.{% else %} `css/style.css` is the whole
  UI — no build step, no framework, edit it directly.{% endif %}
{% if worker != "none" %}
- `src/{{ package_name }}/worker.py` — **the** {{ worker }} entrypoint:
  broker/app setup, importing every `tasks/` module so the worker
  process can discover them. Don't rename or move it.
- `src/{{ package_name }}/tasks/` — **one module per background job.**
  `example.py` is the demo; a new task is a new file here plus one
  import line in `worker.py` (see the comment there for why).
{% endif %}
- `src/{{ package_name }}/core/` — shared infrastructure every
  route/task might depend on: `config.py` (`Settings`, always),
  `templates.py` (the shared `Jinja2Templates` instance, always), {% if database != "none" %}`db.py`
  (async engine/session), {% endif %}{% if redis %}`redis.py` (the `redis_client`), {% endif %}and
  the natural home for anything similar later (e.g. a scheduler). Add
  new config fields to `Settings`, not scattered `os.environ` reads.
{% if database != "none" %}
- `src/{{ package_name }}/models.py` — {{ orm }} models. Fine as one file
  for one resource, free to become `models/` later.
{% endif %}
{% if migrations %}
- `alembic/` — migrations. New model → `uv run alembic revision
  --autogenerate -m "..."`, review the generated file, then `uv run
  alembic upgrade head`.
{% endif %}
- `tests/` — pytest tests{% if database != "none" %} against an
  isolated in-memory SQLite database via a `get_session` override in
  `tests/conftest.py` — the production database is never touched by
  the test suite{% endif %}.

## Conventions

- Dependencies are managed with `uv` via `pyproject.toml` — don't hand-edit
  `uv.lock`; run `uv add <package>` / `uv remove <package>` instead.
- A route that changes state (create/toggle/delete) returns the HTML
  fragment for **just what changed** — never the whole page, and never
  JSON. `hx-target`/`hx-swap` on the triggering element decide where
  that fragment lands; see `templates/index.html` and
  `templates/partials/todo_item.html` for the pattern (including the
  `hx-swap-oob="delete"` trick `todo_created.html` uses to remove the
  empty-state message on the first successful create).
- New HTTP endpoints go in `routes/`, new background jobs go in
  `tasks/`, new shared infrastructure goes in `core/` — don't put any of
  these in `main.py`/`worker.py` themselves, which stay thin entrypoints.
{% if database != "none" %}
- New endpoints that touch the database take `session` via
  `Depends(get_session)` — don't create engines/sessions ad hoc.
{% endif %}

